<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/media-literacy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ERIC scope note: The ability to communicate competently in all media forms, print and electronic, as well as to access, understand, analyze and evaluate the images, words, and sounds that make up mass media messages" <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/media-literacy/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/media-literacy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/Definition> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/media-literacy/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/media-literacy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "The ability to access, interpret, evaluate, and create messages across different forms of media." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/media-literacy/versions/1> .
